## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE)
*Blocker:* a path outside the two; a non-comment byte of `ci.yml` changed; a new pattern that accepts a different token, a shorter token run or an empty match; a row deleted, skipped, retitled away or weakened (a tolerance the old pattern had and the new one lost); an `it(` or `expect(` removed without a replacement of the same assertion; a product string added; lint, typecheck, build, `audit-dev`, `check-shards` or the whole `npm test` red from the head; a reader of `ci.yml` red from the head; a secret; a non-ASCII byte or a person's name in an added line or the message. *Major:* a builder claim your numbers contradict (the NOT rows fail-open at the base, the red-at-base or green-at-head counts, 4102/0/0, 132 tests, the hosted count 14 in 2 files, 32 new rows); a required plant whose red differs from the stated one or stays green; a count or list that can drift unseen (the `REFLOW` table against `PIN`); the comment's number not equal to your `--list` output. *Minor:* a "needing neither" row that a reflow or a comment can fool (unrecorded gap); a weak `refused` list (does not test the boundary of its pattern); a plant of yours green in every row (missing pin, with the cell); a missed tolerance at a token boundary (the old pattern was not tolerant there either). *Note:* `(gate B124 N-1)` dropped from `ci.yml:415` (the builder's kit forbade a `B###` token in an added line); the comment line 416 is 135 characters; e2e shards, dotnet, SQL Server shards, `validate.sh`, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN (landing conditions); the reflow rows test fixture strings, the real-source proof is the plants; UAT held by the product owner and not touched; no formatter exists in `web/`, so no formatter was run. **GO** = steps 0-7 measured, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor/Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major.

